---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import FeedbackEmigrationGame from "../../components/FeedbackEmigrationGame.svelte";
import Header from "../../components/Header.svelte";
import { changelog } from "../../js/emegration-changelog";

const VERSION = changelog[0].version;

const ID = "emigration";
const FILES_PATH = `/files/${ID}/v${VERSION}/`;

let printAndPlay = [
  {
    name: 'Rulebook',
    title: `${ID}-game-rulebook-v${VERSION}.pdf`,
    pages: '25 pages'
  },
  {
    name: 'Mini Cards',
    title: `${ID}-game-mini-cards-v${VERSION}.pdf`,
    pages: '8 pages'
  },
  {
    name: 'Small Square Cards',
    title: `${ID}-game-small-square-cards-v${VERSION}.pdf`,
    pages: '1 page'
  },
  {
    name: 'Medium Chits (optional)',
    title: `${ID}-game-medium-chits-v${VERSION}.pdf`,
    pages: '1 page'
  },
  {
    name: 'Small Chits (optional)',
    title: `${ID}-game-small-chits-v${VERSION}.pdf`,
    pages: '1 page'
  },
];
---

<Header client:idle />
<Layout title="Emigration Board Game">
  <main
    class="max-w-screen-md w-full text-left m-auto px-2 pb-8 font-publicSans"
  >
    <div class="my-4">
      <picture>
        <source
          srcset="/files/emigration/Emigration-Game-Logo.webp"
          type="image/webp"
        />
        <source
          srcset="/files/emigration/Emigration-Game-Logo.png"
          type="image/png"
        />
        <img
          src="/files/emigration/Emigration-Game-Logo.png"
          alt="Emigration Game Logo"
        />
      </picture>
      <p class="uppercase tracking-widest text-center">A board game about moving abroad</p>
      <div
        class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 justify-center items-center mb-4 opacity-50"
      >
        <p>2-6 Players</p>
        <p>20-60 Minutes</p>
        <p>Ages 12+</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    
    <p
      class="mt-4 text-4xl uppercase tracking-widest font-bold break-words text-red-500 text-center"
    >
      Prototype
    </p>

    <p class="px-4 py-2 w-fit mx-auto mb-2">
      Version {VERSION} - <a
        href="/emigration/changelog"
        class="underline">View Changelog</a
      >
    </p>

    <p class="my-4 text-lg">
      You're moving to another country! Scramble to collect documents, make
      valuable connections, and manage your money as life happens. Then pick a
      border control line and hope the officer lets you in!
    </p>

    <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 mt-8 mb-4 justify-center items-center">
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-2 justify-center items-start">

        <div class="inline-flex flex-col gap-2 my-4 items-start">
      <h2 class="font-bold text-2xl">Print & Play Downloads</h2>

      {printAndPlay.map((item) => (
          <a href={FILES_PATH + item.title} download={item.title} class="btn"
                  ><svg
                      xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                      fill="none"
                      viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                      stroke-width="1.5"
                      stroke="currentColor"
                      class="w-6 h-6 flex-none"
                  >
                      <path
                          stroke-linecap="round"
                          stroke-linejoin="round"
                          d="M3 16.5v2.25A2.25 2.25 0 005.25 21h13.5A2.25 2.25 0 0021 18.75V16.5M16.5 12L12 16.5m0 0L7.5 12m4.5 4.5V3"
                      />
                  </svg>
                  {item.name} - {item.pages}</a
              >
      ))}

          <div class="inline-flex flex-col gap-2 my-2 text-left">
              <p class="">
                  To Print & Play, you'll need a printer and some time to cut out all
                  the cards. You'll also need <span class="font-black">One Six-Sided Die</span>.
                 If you don't print the optional Small and Medium Chits, you'll need Money (about 20 per player) and Assurance  (about 10 per player); you can use a different game's pieces for those. 
              </p>
          </div>
  </div>

  <div class="my-4 text-left p-4 bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 rounded-md">
      <h2 class="text-xl tracking-widest font-thin mb-2">Q&A</h2>
      <p class="font-bold">Where can I buy the game?</p>
      <p>
        You can't buy the game yet. But you can print the game yourself and give
        feedback to help with the development.
      </p>

      <p class="font-bold mt-4">How can I ask a question or give feedback?</p>
      <p>
        Use the feedback form at the bottom of this webpage,
        <a
          href="https://discord.gg/aDV6NY73H2"
          target="_blank"
          class="underline cursor-pointer">join the Discord Server</a
        >, or email feedback@tandagames.com.
      </p>
    </div>

        

        <div
          class="text-left inline-flex flex-col justify-center items-center gap-4"
        >
          <div class="bg-neutral-100 p-4 dark:bg-neutral-700 w-full rounded-md">
            <h2 class="text-xl tracking-widest font-thin mb-2">
              Known Elements Needing Further Analysis
            </h2>
            <ul class="list-disc ml-8">
              <li>
                <span class="font-bold">
                  Player count effect on the number of Assurance gained.
                </span> Is the game weighted towards a certain number of players?
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="font-bold"
                  >Optimal (or suboptimal) Life Card combinations.</span
                > What are the best (or worst) Life Cards to use for different types
                of game dynamics and number of players? (For example, what Life Cards&#8212;when
                used together&#8212;encourage wealth building, cutthroat competition,
                friendly play, or drastic events? Or what Life Card combinations
                do not work well together?)
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="font-bold">Game-breaking strategies.</span> Are there
                any strategies which always create predictable outcomes or ruin the
                game for other players? (For example, maybe always discarding Documents
                and Connections instead of buying them always gets you more Assurance than not.)
              </li>
            </ul>
            <p class="my-2">
              If you can help analyze any of these game elements, or have any
              other observations, please share your feedback using the form
              below, <a
                href="https://discord.gg/aDV6NY73H2"
                target="_blank"
                class="underline cursor-pointer"
                >by joining the Discord Server</a
              >, or by sending an email to feedback@tandagames.com (you can
              include your name if you want to be publicly credited with
              helping develop the game). Thank you!
            </p>
            <p class="italic my-2">Updated November 10, 2022</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <FeedbackEmigrationGame
      title="Playtester's Feedback"
      client:visible
      expand={true}
      discordLink="https://discord.gg/aDV6NY73H2"
      version={VERSION}
      changelog={changelog}
    />
  </main>
</Layout>
